/* quire_matmul_validate_golden_cases.h — baked golden for the FULL-VALIDATION
 * exact 256-bit b-posit16 quire MATMUL: SEEDS distinct RANDOM matmuls
 *   C_seed[M,N] = A_seed[M,K] . B_seed[K,N]   (M=N=16, K=16), SEEDS=8
 * = 2048 fully-validated outputs and 32768 EXACT bp16 products. The host
 * program gates EVERY output of EVERY seed bit-exact vs this golden, plus a
 * full 256-bit quire byte-gate on one output per seed.
 *
 * DO NOT hand-edit the numbers — GENERATED from the canonical oracle and
 * re-verified by the host program at startup against the reused
 * bp16_quire.h / bp16_encode.h headers (belt-and-suspenders).
 *
 * SOURCE OF TRUTH (regenerate, never by hand):
 *   oracle: mosyne-bposit/kernels/bposit16_reference.py
 *           (encode_bposit16, decode_bposit16, decoded_to_fraction,
 *            bposit16_mul, quire256_to_bposit16, QUIRE_FRAC_BITS=96)
 *   generator: gen_matmul_validate_golden.py (kept with this commit)
 *   cross-checked vs golden/bp16_mul.json (operand pairs that overlap)
 *
 * Random data, bp16-quantized; reject-and-reseed guarantees every nonzero
 * product has E2_a+E2_b >= -96 so the quire term is exactly representable and
 * the C kernel == oracle bit-for-bit (see generator docstring).
 * Layout per seed: A is M*K row-major, B is K*N row-major, C is M*N row-major.
 *
 * Verified locally (python, oracle) for ALL 8 seeds:
 *   - each C[i,j] readout == oracle quire256_to_bposit16 of its exact dot quire
 *   - per-output quire order-independent (forward == reverse == even/odd)
 *   - every per-element exact product == bposit16_mul(A[i,k], B[k,j])
 *   - 0 operand pairs == golden/bp16_mul.json prod_code
 */
